            <div xml:id="d651">

                <pb facs="0791" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/209</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The French Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Claudel</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-10">December 10, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: Referring to the
                    conversation which I had with you recently, relative to the question of
                    extraterritoriality in China, I have the honor to send herewith to Your
                    Excellency a résumé of the instructions which were sent by the Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs of the Republic to the Minister of France in China [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">French Ambassador in London</hi>].</p>
                <p>In addition, Your Excellency will also find enclosed a copy of a note addressed
                    on November 25, 1929, by the Ministry of Foreign <pb facs="0792" n="648"
                        xml:id="pg648"/> Affairs to the Embassy of Great Britain at Paris, in reply
                    to a memorandum from the latter. This note sums up the whole French viewpoint in
                    the question of extraterritoriality.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Claudel</hi></signed></closer>



